  nation: USA
  group: upgradeable
  category: tech_tree
  status: released
notes:
  - "Bearing is the target's direction from the bow, clockwise: 0 bow, 90 starboard, 180 stern, 270 port. Bow is 331-29, stern 151-209, starboard 30-150, port 210-330. The target is distant, so every mount sees it at the same bearing; mount positions on the hull are ignored. Each arc's salvo is at the bearing inside it where the most damage bears, nearest the arc's centre on a tie."
  - "Fire figures assume every bearing shell hits and the guns fire at their reload. fires_per_minute = 60 / reload_s x barrels bearing x p, summed over mounts. With a target, p is the shell's fire chance times the target's fire_chance_factor (its hull's fire-node probability, lower at higher tiers, times its build's burnProb, e.g. x0.9 with Fire Prevention Expert), capped at 100%. Not applied: the fire limit (target fire_zones fires at once), fire duration and the Damage Control Party consumable."
  - "No target ship: p is the shell's fire chance alone. The target's hull and build lower it (x0.5005 on a tier 10 hull); give target_ship to apply them."
  - "Dispersion is the main battery shell ellipse at the range. How many shells hit depends on the target's size, angle and the aim point; this tool does not estimate hits."
